    {
      "x": 620,
      "y": 1290,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-pass",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 1080,
        "h": 280,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "green",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "PASS WHEN every arrow starts and ends on a port — there is no line between two card middles any more. Ports on a wall spread across the whole wall rather than clustering in one section, and no label is struck through by another. ARROW changes every cable in the region; a single selected cable still changes on its own. A socket dragged in Communication stays put when you flip to Dataflow and back."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "a8xqU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 100,
      "y": 520,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-2",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 420,
        "h": 170,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2 · Press Service, drag Mission's card onto Robot's. No ports, no port dots. Repeat with Action. Then Stream, Camera → Mission."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "a3rHn",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "z": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "camera:page:page",
      "typeName": "camera"
    },
    {
      "x": 100,
      "y": 750,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-3",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 420,
        "h": 190,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3 · CABLES › Split. One arrow becomes its protocol legs, each tagged with its phase. Summary puts them back — it always rides the request, or the goal."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "a4MZb",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 320,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-4",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 420,
        "h": 180,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4 · Press Dataflow. Cards go Port, cables go Data, and every socket is back on a left or right lane — Dataflow has no top or bottom edge."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "a5vb6",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 560,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-5",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 420,
        "h": 200,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 12,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5 · ARROW › Curve, then Straight. Every cable in the region changes shape at once, and one undo puts them all back. A single cable still takes its own shape from its selection menu."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "a6ez5",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    {
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 860,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:cue-step-6",
      "type": "geo",
      "props": {
        "w": 420,
        "h": 210,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "draw",
        "growY": 2,
        "url": "",
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "color": "orange",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6 · CARD › P, then press and HOLD a port dot and drag it to any of the four edges. Or select the port and use the inspector's Block edge control. Hold still first — moving straight away draws a cable."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "a7PUJ",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
